BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 278.30 Tm (Section 3: Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.07 Tm (The sharpest split on the street is the knowledge bar. Amanda Lockaby tells prospective relators that the key is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.85 Tm (demonstrating intentional fraud and that mistakes or negligence are not enough [OfdepsSYjp4 @ 00:01:29]. Mark) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.62 Tm (Kleiman runs the opposite playbook. In his reading the statute says intent to defraud is not required, reckless disregard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 210.40 Tm (and deliberate indifference are enough, and in practice the bar sits near gross negligence [yN7NRjwYKFs @ 00:31:35].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.17 Tm (Maryanne Hamilton and Darth Newman side with Kleiman. They frame the Act as no negligence statute that also) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.95 Tm (carries no intent-to-defraud requirement, and their classic proof is a biller who objects and is told "just do it that way.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.72 Tm (That's how we get paid" [HocnawRgrAA @ 00:19:55]. Andrew Hillman reads the knowingly definition the same way,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.50 Tm (folding in deliberate ignorance and reckless disregard, and states that no proof of specific intent to defraud is required) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 134.27 Tm ([AcMsQCQm5QI @ 00:01:54]. The split drives intake screening. A Lockaby-style intake rejects sloppy-billing files) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.05 Tm (that a Kleiman-style intake pushes forward when the paper trail shows someone was warned and kept billing anyway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.82 Tm (Teams on the reckless-disregard threshold work a wider pipeline of files built on warnings that were ignored. Teams) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 88.60 Tm (anchored on intentional fraud run a narrower docket and pass on cases built only on carelessness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 73.37 Tm (Money splits are the second fault line. Against The Fraud pitches a flat 15 to 30 percent and treats first-to-file as) Tj ET
