BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 493.77 Tm (The most expensive self-inflicted wound is the evidence grab. In Cafasso, the relator took 11 GB, the NDA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 478.55 Tm (counterclaim was upheld, and $300,000 in fees was awarded; the account of how it happened is damning on its own: "i) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 463.32 Tm (just grabbed the whole folder um she didn't read the files she just read the file names" [JN4iipJiHZM @ 00:11:12].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.10 Tm (Mike Paulus confirms defense clients pursue counterclaims for improper access, and the panel flags that "rummaging") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 432.87 Tm (is a factor and that the CFAA criminalizes unauthorized access, so the better play is telling the government where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 417.65 Tm (documents sit so it can subpoena them [JN4iipJiHZM @ 00:09:12]. Privilege is the second trap: David Wiseman warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 402.42 Tm (that privileged productions delay DOJ, force taint review, and can disqualify the attorneys assigned [JN4iipJiHZM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.20 Tm (00:07:36]. Mary Ann Hamilton draws the same line from the relator side: never take documents you would not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.97 Tm (normally access, be targeted, avoid work email and work machines, and never feed case data to AI because it is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 356.75 Tm (privileged, can be subpoenaed, and gives wrong legal answers [H0ay64A0XXA @ 00:10:52]. Hamilton's verdict on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 341.52 Tm (overreach: it "can very quickly undermine the legitimacy of a case and it can get you in trouble all on its own.") Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 326.30 Tm (Seal breaches and settlement paperwork are where money leaks after the case is already won. The ABA panel stresses) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.07 Tm (that "it's not an automatic dismissal if the relator breaches the seal," but the bill still comes due: in Bibi v. Wells Fargo,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.85 Tm (DOJ recommended $2.7M, the share above the 25 percent minimum, and the court ordered $1.6M [JN4iipJiHZM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 280.62 Tm (00:48:18]. Defendants hit the seal problem too; Mike Paulus says insurers create a catch-22, so Paulus seeks an extra) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 265.40 Tm (partial lift. Sarah Frazier warns that a common reason for a government veto is too much of the settlement allocated to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 250.17 Tm (the retaliation claim, and the panel says to tell DOJ about any retaliation claim in advance [vHZhDg8Ml14 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.95 Tm (00:06:14]. Exit paperwork is the employee-side trap: the McGuireWoods team notes FCA claims cannot be released,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 219.72 Tm (but the recovery can, meaning a departing employee who signs can lose the right to share in any recovery) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 204.50 Tm ([J3hHvouRce8 @ 00:55:28]. Blake Percival lived that trap: severance was $42,000 with a fine-print waiver of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 189.27 Tm (whistleblower rights, and their lawyer's advice was "don't sign anything" [FopC1sCa2y8 @ 00:31:22]. Refusing that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 174.05 Tm ($42,000 kept the path open to the roughly $6M, 20 percent share Percival later received.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.82 Tm (The economics check is time, and every practitioner who has lived a case reports it running longer than planned. Blake) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 143.60 Tm (Percival filed a sealed qui tam on July 1, 2011 through Beasley Allen after being fired in May 2011, then sat through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 128.37 Tm (60-to-90-day continuances for years; a June 2013 hardship settlement attempt was derailed by the Snowden hearings,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 113.15 Tm (and DOJ intervened only on October 30, 2013 [FopC1sCa2y8 @ 00:38:39]. The firing alone cost six figures in pay, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 97.92 Tm ($20K bonus, an SUV and an Amex. The settlement came to about $30M, with Percival taking 20 percent, about $6M,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 82.70 Tm (against fraud that ran across 665,000 investigations and a Wall Street Journal estimate of seven point six billion dollars) Tj ET
