0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Step: 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Title: Clock every incident against the contract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Action: Pre-map each contract's notification window and lock incident data on discovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Detail: Identify whether the contract says 'reasonable time,' 'without undue delay' or a hard 72-hour deadline [Jones) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Day - ah8GhXnbe-8 @ 00:02:05], and preserve everything tied to the incident for at least 90 days [Thompson Coburn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (LLP - CNlX3Qfdluw @ 00:22:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (Step: 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Title: Run the CID and subpoena playbook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Action: Freeze destruction, engage outside counsel and open a channel with DOJ early.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (Detail: On a subpoena or CID, don't panic, call counsel and halt document destruction [PilieroMazza PLLC -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (ZyG_Zu7OvIg @ 00:44:22]; designate a point of contact, issue a litigation hold and line up IT resources) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm ([WilliamsMullen - NdqYGSN5BYc @ 00:54:27]; then stop any ongoing problem, investigate internally and engage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (DOJ early [Cape Endeavors, Inc. - -2BTi30xXrA @ 00:29:21].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (The unit economics are where contractors get blindsided. Zack Trilliger, the former EDVA U.S. Attorney who now) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (runs a firm's DC office, walks the math: damages triple, so $5M becomes $15M, and penalties of $14K to $28K attach) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (to each claim, including every invoice on an IDIQ, before suspension and debarment even enter the picture) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm ([-2BTi30xXrA @ 00:07:24]. Daniel Strauss pushes the base number higher, explaining that on a $1M contract carrying) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm ($100K of profit the government's position is that the full $1M is owed regardless of profit, and treble damages turn it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (into $3M [GkIQylusGaw @ 00:49:01]. PilieroMazza's cyber panel runs the same multiplier on a $10M contract to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (reach a $30M recovery claim [OqheRWaihEo @ 01:07:40]. Matt Feinberg then layers the per-invoice penalty on top:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (60 invoices means 60 violations, a $150K billing error balloons to roughly $475K at about '23,000 a pop,' and a $7M) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (HUBZone contract can generate a whistleblower share of roughly $7M on its own [ZyG_Zu7OvIg @ 00:46:22].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Trilliger's own label for this exposure is 'extinction level events for certain companies.' The operator lesson is to model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (risk per invoice rather than per contract, because the penalty count scales directly with billing frequency, and monthly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (invoicing on a multi-year IDIQ quietly stacks dozens of separate violations onto a single underlying compliance gap.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (The procedural clock is long and lopsided. Bracker notes that the statute gives the government 60 days to investigate,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (which is barely enough to assemble a team and interview the relator; extensions run from three months to a year, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (longest seal Bracker has carried lasted over ten years, and the average case runs two to three years from filing to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (resolution [j_QEFJG-ON4 @ 00:14:44]. On the government's investigative toolkit, Trilliger reports civil investigative) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (demands for both documents and testimony, one of them reaching back seven years across all records, with 30-day or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (14-day turnarounds and a public motion to compel waiting for anyone who ignores them [-2BTi30xXrA @ 00:14:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (The relator economics run on a sliding scale. UAP Legion breaks out 15-25% when DOJ intervenes and 25-30% when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (it declines, so a $300M recovery pays the relator between $45M and $90M, with the first-to-file rule rewarding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (whoever reaches the courthouse first [Y9DOny35SW0 @ 00:13:09]. Sarah Mlan adds that relators collect up to 30%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (plus attorney's fees and that 'you don't actually have to have a lot of information' to qualify [ovf7HOfeGQ0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (00:06:04]. Low evidentiary entry cost, a first-to-file race and a percentage-of-recovery payout mean the relator pipeline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (stays full, and a contractor should assume any known gap is already being documented by someone inside the building.) Tj ET
