0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (If the information came through your role as an attorney or accountant, resolve that before filing or the claim can sit in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (a taint process for three to five years [Brown, LLC - A Premier Whistleblower Law Firm - tQIkb01vCTw @ 00:05:48].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Describe supporting documents you do not hold but know exist, and tell the IRS exactly where to find them [Teach) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Me! Personal Finance - WA3dtUQT9f8 @ 00:02:46].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Plead that the target owes tax; Zerbe says showing fraud is a nice bonus, but all you need to show is that the person) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (owes tax [Kohn Kohn & Colapinto - O45E7FrG_mM @ 00:17:40].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (3. Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (The sharpest split is whether to file Form 211 solo or behind counsel. Emily Stibil of Phillips and Cohen says flatly that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (you don't need a lawyer to file a tip, positioning an attorney as a way to navigate the process and craft the tip so it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (heightens the likelihood of success [fQss6bE5tKc @ 00:00:34]. Jason T. Brown pushes much harder: you can fill out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (the form yourself, but Brown strongly discourages it, predicting a self-filed claim will probably hurt the case and go) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm (into the circular file, while conceding that certain people have recovered without an attorney [RuNrDW46nKY @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (00:12:28]. Alina of Oberhide PC sells counsel as a credibility signal, arguing the IRS has reason to believe law-firm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (submissions are genuine because the firm has already vetted eligibility and substantiation and walks away from cases) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (that fail either test [sNHauc7rutQ @ 00:08:46]. Brown's intake desk shows what the solo route costs: many matters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (arrive after someone already submitted their own Form 211 and wants it salvaged, the firm reviews whether it can even) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (clean up the mess people generally make on their own, and it declines on the spot when it can't [tQIkb01vCTw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (00:06:18]. The working read from the counsel camp is blunt: a botched first filing is treated as close to unrecoverable,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (because you only get one first bite at the apple.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (Case-size doctrine splits into two camps. Former IRS agent Mike Sullivan preaches whales only: the IRS wants a big) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (splash that can make the newspapers and please the commissioner, not a couple of bait fish on top of the water, and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (small or undocumented claim is not worth anyone's time [41ejxu80Qtg @ 00:03:10]. Bryan Skarlatos answers from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (twenty years of whistleblower practice that bigger is not better, reporting many billion-dollar claims filed in a career) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (and none of them paid, because a massive claim drags the IRS into a very complex process [ruRW_hNSDYk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (00:12:43]. Skarlatos expects hundred-million-plus cases to hit headwinds from complexity and well funded taxpayer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (defenses, and puts the sweet spot at 10 to 50 million dollars, or a tighter 10 to 25 million, while warning that a five or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (six million claim may not justify a ten-year wait for a 20 to 30 percent award once professional fees are counted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm ([ruRW_hNSDYk @ 00:16:01]. Eric Green backs the middle path with paid results: the cases that actually paid were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (small, simple income tax evasion matters the government could make and plead out, and Green notes the DOJ side has) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (no patience for complicated RICO-type builds either [ruRW_hNSDYk @ 00:13:20]. Sullivan's whale doctrine and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm (Skarlatos sweet spot agree on one thing only: tiny cases die in the queue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (Routing is the third fault line. Sullivan says IRS Criminal Investigation chases conviction rates and doesn't care if it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 214.80 Tm (collects a nickel, wanting the target behind bars, which is exactly why small payroll or unreported-income gripes go) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (nowhere with that unit [QxVllUQ7IRk @ 00:01:50]. Skarlatos explains that CI is far more used to working with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.35 Tm (witnesses and informants than the civil side, and agrees with Green's practice in the right case: bypass the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.12 Tm (Whistleblower Office, go directly to IRS CI, then lodge the claim with the office before CI acts, because skipping that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 153.90 Tm (filing forfeits the award entirely [ruRW_hNSDYk @ 00:22:37]. Brown hedges the same play, warning that a criminal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.67 Tm (referral might accelerate a case but can increase the risk your identity is revealed or create criminal exposure, a fate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.45 Tm (some other IRS complainants have already suffered, so it is a strategy reserved for a clean whistleblower working it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.22 Tm (through counsel [tQIkb01vCTw @ 00:03:58]. Dean Zerbe sets a lower proof bar than the criminal-first crowd: you just) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 93.00 Tm (need to show the target owes tax, and proving fraud is a nice bonus rather than a requirement [O45E7FrG_mM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 77.77 Tm (00:17:40]. The criminal-first operators trade exposure risk for speed and traction, while the civil filers accept slower,) Tj ET
